# Homepage visual

## Hero photos

Two on the left, three on the right. Text sits in the wide center column.

- **Main photo** on each side: vertically centered, the large one, overflowing past the outer edge of the frame. Top and bottom stay in frame.
- **Secondary photos**: smaller, toward the text, off that vertical center. Not lined up with the main photo.
- The five photos are a mock for now (Wanderlust, Čajový dýchánek, Zahrádkářská kolonie, Advent a Vánoce, Svatba Mlhových).
- The side-by-side collage is for screens 1200px and wider. Below that the hero stacks: left photos, text, right photos. Phones keep the full-bleed prints. From 801px to 1199px each cluster is centered and capped (`40rem`) so the poster stays about one screen tall, and the smaller prints stay on that photo.

## Every homepage photo

- Keep the file’s aspect ratio. Never stretch, squash, or crop to a new ratio (`height: auto`, no fixed height, no `object-fit: cover`). Overflow past the side is position only.
- Hero prints and section photos have a drop shadow from above: pronounced, with a wide spread, so it reads on the greige.
- Tilt at most **0.5deg**. Neighbors lean opposite ways.
- A **1px** corner radius. No border, no white mat, no entrance or hover animation.

## Ground

- Header and footer stay **white**. Hero and the three section plots are `$color-greige` (pale, low saturation).
- Separate those blocks, including the three columns, with **.75rem** of the white page. No hairlines.
- The hero is only as tall as its photos, with clear top and bottom padding. The poster on the left sets that height.

## Hero text

Featured item is the next published current or upcoming event, else the latest post. Centered: kicker, title, place and date, a short summary (opening of the body, about 220 characters), and a **Připoj se** button. Title is upright Fraunces, larger than the body, not huge.

## Section plots

The three work sections only (not Události). One photo and centered text. Section titles start with a capital letter (Svatební rituály, Himmelhaus, Umění). Rituály and Umění put the photo on top; Himmelhaus puts it on the bottom. The photo runs past that outer edge, far enough that its tilt does not open a gap, and the block clips the picture and its shadow. Three columns from 1200px, with the same .75rem white gap. Stacked below that. The outer-edge crop is `2.25rem` until 1280px, then `4.25rem`.
